From 723cc3f3813858186fe93c663441d75f762be8d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Varun-iiitb <var3907@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 02:44:37 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 46/68] F15: an identity rejection at the password login counts
 as a failed login; an Error refuses (task 19 review)

- Before this fix, a rejected identity check was not counted anywhere: the password step had already reset the
  user's failed attempts. Someone with the password could probe faces without limit, logging in again after every two
  rejected attempts. LivenessApi.verifyIdentity now records a failed login (LoginService.recordFailedLoginAttempt, the
  counter behind the login lockout) for a rejection on the first attempt of the password_login gate.
  - The rule is IdentityBinding.countsAsFailedLogin. It counts once per login, also when the retry is then cancelled
    or rejected again.
  - Packet authentication and supervisor approval are not counted, as on Desktop, where only the login counts.
- An Error thrown while checking (for example out of memory on a malformed template) used to kill the worker before
  the Pigeon result was posted, so the gate waited forever. It now gives a refusal: outcome ERROR, not accepted, not
  retryable.

Test: IdentityBindingTest counts the first rejection at the login once, and never counts an accepted check, a second
attempt, or the other gates. 113 module tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
